flowchart TB
    accTitle: Alternative selection methods
    accDescr: A proposed candidate set with assigned values can be passed to different selection methods. Examples named by CoALA are argmax, softmax, majority vote, and other suitable alternatives. These are alternatives, not sequential steps.

    INPUT[Candidate set and assigned values]
    subgraph METHODS[Possible selection methods]
      direction LR
      ARGMAX[Argmax<br/>maximum represented value]
      SOFTMAX[Softmax<br/>value-sensitive distribution]
      VOTE[Majority vote<br/>voting-based choice]
      OTHER[Other suitable method]
    end
    OUT[Selection outcome<br/>select an action or reject the set]
    INPUT --> METHODS
    ARGMAX --> OUT
    SOFTMAX --> OUT
    VOTE --> OUT
    OTHER --> OUT

    classDef process fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef option fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    classDef result fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.4px;
    class INPUT process;
    class ARGMAX,SOFTMAX,VOTE,OTHER option;
    class OUT result;
